      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n21: project with Tantack-Query: \nI learnt tantack query, for api call tantack query paly very important\nrole, it's provide isloading, data, cache so when we call normal api then\nit's call and again when we change every route or page. tantack query solve\nthis problem it's call api only once and when change page differnet page it's \nstore cache of api, so it's not call again api. also we can provide staleTime\nfor call again api.  that we use tanstack query for api call. first i install \ntanstack using npm i @tanstack/react-query. then in main.jsx file\nwrapped approutes.jsx to <QueryProvider client={queryClient> <AppRoutes/>\nand imported this statement import {\n  useQuery,\n  useMutation,\n  useQueryClient,\n  QueryClient,\n  QueryClientProvider,\n} from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\n// Create a client\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient();\n\n\nand then on productHook.jsx file i wrote this code for api call using tanstack.\n\nimport { useQuery } from \"@tanstack/react-query\"\nimport { getProductsDataApi } from \"../api/productApi\"\n\nexport const useProductApi = () => {\n    const {isPending, data, error} = useQuery({\n        queryKey: ['products'],\n        queryFn: getProductsDataApi,\n        staleTime: 30000\n    })\n    return {\n        isPending, data, error\n    }\n}\n\n\nI create config folder inside a create axiosInstance.jsx file for axios instance\nand provide this code: \nimport axios from \"axios\";\n\nexport const axiosInstance = axios.create({\n    baseURL: \"https://dummyjson.com\"\n})\n\n\nafter that: \n\nI called api from tanstack query and show all product data inside shop.page \nusing productCard.jsx component. \n\nimport axios from \"axios\";\nimport ProductCard from \"../components/ProductCard\";\nimport ProductCardSkeleton from \"../components/ProductCardSkeleton\";\nimport { useProductApi } from \"../hooks/productHook\";\nimport Filters from \"../components/Filters\";\nimport { useFilter } from \"../hooks/filterHook\";\n\nconst ShopPage = () => {\n  const {filteredProducts, filterProducts, isLoading\n  } = useFilter();\n\n  const {isPending, data, error} = useProductApi()\n  if (error) return <h1>{error.message}</h1>\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"flex flex-col gap-5\">\n      <Filters filterProducts={filterProducts}/>\n      {isPending ? (\n        <div className=\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 place-items-center gap-6\">\n          {Array.from({ length: 8 }).map((_, index) => (\n            <ProductCardSkeleton key={index} />\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      ) : (\n        <div className=\"grid px-4 grid-cols-1  sm:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4 lg:grid-cols-3 place-items-center gap-6\">\n          {filteredProducts.map((product) => (\n            <ProductCard key={product.id} product={product} />\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default ShopPage;\n\n\nthis is a ProductCard.jsx component code: \nconst ProductCard = ({ product }) => {\n  const isInStock = product.stock > 0;\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"group relative w-full max-w-sm rounded-xl p-[1px] overflow-hidden bg-transparent hover:bg-gradient-to-r hover:from-purple-500 hover:via-pink-500 hover:to-blue-500 transition-all duration-500\">\n      \n      {/* Card */}\n      <div className=\"relative bg-[#111111] rounded-xl overflow-hidden\">\n        \n        {/* Product Image */}\n        <div className=\"w-full h-56 bg-[#181818]\">\n          <img\n            src={product.thumbnail}\n            alt={product.title}\n            className=\"w-full h-full object-contain group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500\"\n          />\n        </div>\n\n        {/* Product Details */}\n        <div className=\"p-5\">\n\n          {/* Category + Stock */}\n          <div className=\"flex items-center justify-between mb-2\">\n            <p className=\"text-sm text-gray-400 font-medium capitalize\">\n              {product.category}\n            </p>\n\n            <span\n              className={`text-sm font-medium ${\n                isInStock ? \"text-green-400\" : \"text-red-400\"\n              }`}\n            >\n              {isInStock\n                ? `In Stock (${product.stock})`\n                : \"Out of Stock\"}\n            </span>\n          </div>\n\n          {/* Title */}\n          <h2 className=\"text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-5 line-clamp-1\">\n            {product.title}\n          </h2>\n\n          {/* Price + Button */}\n          <div className=\"flex items-center justify-between\">\n\n            {/* Price */}\n            <span className=\"text-2xl font-bold text-white\">\n              ${product.price}\n            </span>\n\n            {/* Add To Cart */}\n            <button\n              disabled={!isInStock}\n              onClick={() => console.log(\"Added to cart:\", product)}\n              className={`px-4 text-lg py-2 rounded-lg font-medium transition-all duration-300 ${\n                isInStock\n                  ? \"bg-purple-600 text-white hover:bg-purple-500 hover:shadow-[0_0_20px_rgba(168,85,247,0.5)]\"\n                  : \"bg-[#2a2a2a] text-gray-500 cursor-not-allowed\"\n              }`}\n            >\n              {isInStock ? \"Add to Cart\" : \"Out of Stock\"}\n            </button>\n\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default ProductCard;\n\n\nI implement filter for when user serach using search bar then product\nshow on shop.page that user searched. \n\n                 ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n21: project with Tantack-Query: \nI learnt tantack query, for api call tantack query paly very important\nrole, it's provide isloading, data, cache so when we call normal api then\nit's call and again when we change every route or page. tantack query solve\nthis problem it's call api only once and when change page differnet page it's \nstore cache of api, so it's not call again api. also we can provide staleTime\nfor call again api.  that we use tanstack query for api call. first i install \ntanstack using npm i @tanstack/react-query. then in main.jsx file\nwrapped approutes.jsx to <QueryProvider client={queryClient> <AppRoutes/>\nand imported this statement import {\n  useQuery,\n  useMutation,\n  useQueryClient,\n  QueryClient,\n  QueryClientProvider,\n} from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\n// Create a client\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient();\n\n\nand then on productHook.jsx file i wrote this code for api call using tanstack.\n\nimport { useQuery } from \"@tanstack/react-query\"\nimport { getProductsDataApi } from \"../api/productApi\"\n\nexport const useProductApi = () => {\n    const {isPending, data, error} = useQuery({\n        queryKey: ['products'],\n        queryFn: getProductsDataApi,\n        staleTime: 30000\n    })\n    return {\n        isPending, data, error\n    }\n}\n\n\nI create config folder inside a create axiosInstance.jsx file for axios instance\nand provide this code: \nimport axios from \"axios\";\n\nexport const axiosInstance = axios.create({\n    baseURL: \"https://dummyjson.com\"\n})\n\n\nafter that: \n\nI called api from tanstack query and show all product data inside shop.page \nusing productCard.jsx component. \n\nimport axios from \"axios\";\nimport ProductCard from \"../components/ProductCard\";\nimport ProductCardSkeleton from \"../components/ProductCardSkeleton\";\nimport { useProductApi } from \"../hooks/productHook\";\nimport Filters from \"../components/Filters\";\nimport { useFilter } from \"../hooks/filterHook\";\n\nconst ShopPage = () => {\n  const {filteredProducts, filterProducts, isLoading\n  } = useFilter();\n\n  const {isPending, data, error} = useProductApi()\n  if (error) return <h1>{error.message}</h1>\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"flex flex-col gap-5\">\n      <Filters filterProducts={filterProducts}/>\n      {isPending ? (\n        <div className=\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 place-items-center gap-6\">\n          {Array.from({ length: 8 }).map((_, index) => (\n            <ProductCardSkeleton key={index} />\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      ) : (\n        <div className=\"grid px-4 grid-cols-1  sm:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4 lg:grid-cols-3 place-items-center gap-6\">\n          {filteredProducts.map((product) => (\n            <ProductCard key={product.id} product={product} />\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default ShopPage;\n\n\nthis is a ProductCard.jsx component code: \nconst ProductCard = ({ product }) => {\n  const isInStock = product.stock > 0;\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"group relative w-full max-w-sm rounded-xl p-[1px] overflow-hidden bg-transparent hover:bg-gradient-to-r hover:from-purple-500 hover:via-pink-500 hover:to-blue-500 transition-all duration-500\">\n      \n      {/* Card */}\n      <div className=\"relative bg-[#111111] rounded-xl overflow-hidden\">\n        \n        {/* Product Image */}\n        <div className=\"w-full h-56 bg-[#181818]\">\n          <img\n            src={product.thumbnail}\n            alt={product.title}\n            className=\"w-full h-full object-contain group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500\"\n          />\n        </div>\n\n        {/* Product Details */}\n        <div className=\"p-5\">\n\n          {/* Category + Stock */}\n          <div className=\"flex items-center justify-between mb-2\">\n            <p className=\"text-sm text-gray-400 font-medium capitalize\">\n              {product.category}\n            </p>\n\n            <span\n              className={`text-sm font-medium ${\n                isInStock ? \"text-green-400\" : \"text-red-400\"\n              }`}\n            >\n              {isInStock\n                ? `In Stock (${product.stock})`\n                : \"Out of Stock\"}\n            </span>\n          </div>\n\n          {/* Title */}\n          <h2 className=\"text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-5 line-clamp-1\">\n            {product.title}\n          </h2>\n\n          {/* Price + Button */}\n          <div className=\"flex items-center justify-between\">\n\n            {/* Price */}\n            <span className=\"text-2xl font-bold text-white\">\n              ${product.price}\n            </span>\n\n            {/* Add To Cart */}\n            <button\n              disabled={!isInStock}\n              onClick={() => console.log(\"Added to cart:\", product)}\n              className={`px-4 text-lg py-2 rounded-lg font-medium transition-all duration-300 ${\n                isInStock\n                  ? \"bg-purple-600 text-white hover:bg-purple-500 hover:shadow-[0_0_20px_rgba(168,85,247,0.5)]\"\n                  : \"bg-[#2a2a2a] text-gray-500 cursor-not-allowed\"\n              }`}\n            >\n              {isInStock ? \"Add to Cart\" : \"Out of Stock\"}\n            </button>\n\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default ProductCard;\n\n\nI implement filter for when user serach using search bar then product\nshow on shop.page that user searched. \n\n                 ",
